\subsection{\code{BaseRMosaicLayerProcessor$recorded_table()}}{
  The two-way table the call was handed, when it is one.

Only a two-dimensional table is read. \code{mosaicplot()} accepts three and
more, splitting recursively, and a \code{mosaic} layer has one category
axis and one fill -- so a deeper table has nowhere to put its later
dimensions and is declined rather than flattened into a
cross-classification the chart does not claim.
